  - eyebrow: "Why It Matters"
    heading: "Healthcare Raises The Bar, Not Lowers It"
    body: "In most software categories, an overconfident AI feature is an inconvenience. In healthcare, an overconfident AI feature can shape a decision that affects someone's health. That is why we are deliberate about what we claim our technology can do, and equally deliberate about naming what it cannot do yet. A system that cannot explain its own limitations has not earned the trust required to be used in healthcare contexts."
